WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.900 --> 00:00:07.959
Installing PageMotor on A2 Hosting. It is standard cPanel, about ten minutes, and you do not need to be technical.

2
00:00:08.659 --> 00:00:15.269
Getting to cPanel takes one extra hop here. Sign in at my.a2hosting.com, go to My Accounts,

3
00:00:15.269 --> 00:00:22.968
click Manage next to your hosting package, and then click Login to Control Panel on the hosting dashboard.

4
00:00:22.968 --> 00:00:28.489
That opens cPanel, and everything after this is the standard set of screens.

5
00:00:29.189 --> 00:00:37.566
In cPanel, open File Manager and go to the folder for your site, which for your main domain is public_html.

6
00:00:37.566 --> 00:00:42.106
Click Upload, choose the PageMotor zip, and let it finish.

7
00:00:42.106 --> 00:00:49.309
Then right-click the zip, choose Extract, and delete the zip afterwards to keep things tidy.

8
00:00:49.309 --> 00:00:55.102
You should end up with pagemotor.php, a lib folder, and config-sample.php.

9
00:00:55.802 --> 00:01:00.380
The database is where A2 is a little kinder than most cPanel hosts.

10
00:01:00.380 --> 00:01:08.922
Rather than three separate stages on one page, it gives you the MySQL Database Wizard, which walks the whole job in one pass:

11
00:01:08.922 --> 00:01:16.096
name the database, create the user with a generated password, and on the last screen tick ALL PRIVILEGES.

12
00:01:16.796 --> 00:01:23.390
One thing to watch as you go through it. A2 prefixes the database with your account name automatically,

13
00:01:23.390 --> 00:01:30.177
so what you type as pagemotor is saved as something like accountname_pagemotor, and the user the same way.

14
00:01:30.177 --> 00:01:37.091
The full name shown at the end of the wizard is the one to copy. Take the username and the password with it.

15
00:01:37.791 --> 00:01:46.164
Then rename config-sample.php to exactly config.php. That rename is what switches PageMotor on.

16
00:01:46.164 --> 00:01:53.392
Put your three values in, exactly as the wizard showed them, including the prefix.

17
00:01:53.392 --> 00:02:00.268
DB_HOST stays localhost, which is correct for every A2 Hosting cPanel account.

18
00:02:00.968 --> 00:02:09.716
Then go straight to /admin/. On that first visit PageMotor sets itself up and walks you into creating your admin user.

19
00:02:09.716 --> 00:02:13.646
Open the admin before you open the front of the site.

20
00:02:14.346 --> 00:02:18.830
Now something specific to A2 that looks like a fault and is not.

21
00:02:18.830 --> 00:02:30.670
If your plan is one of the Turbo tiers, it runs LiteSpeed with heavy caching, and on the very first visits after installation LiteSpeed needs a moment to warm its cache.

22
00:02:30.670 --> 00:02:34.524
The site will feel slow. That is normal, and it passes.

23
00:02:34.524 --> 00:02:42.581
If it is still slow after the first few minutes, check that the cache is enabled under LiteSpeed Web Cache Manager.

24
00:02:43.281 --> 00:02:52.092
If you hit a 500 or a blank page, it is almost always config.php: wrong name, wrong folder, or never renamed.

25
00:02:52.092 --> 00:02:58.235
There are two places to read the real reason on A2. cPanel, Metrics, Errors.

26
00:02:58.235 --> 00:03:06.965
And an error_log file that A2 writes into public_html itself, which you can open straight from File Manager.

27
00:03:07.665 --> 00:03:12.898
And if the log says “MySQLi Connection Error”, that is actually good news.

28
00:03:12.898 --> 00:03:17.566
It means config.php is working and PageMotor reached the database.

29
00:03:17.566 --> 00:03:23.223
Re-check the prefixed names, the password, and that the user has all privileges.

